{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"997c9ef4-a161-4391-95b5-27a50afea54b","title":"Angles in a triangle add up to 180 degrees"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"997c9ef4-a161-4391-95b5-27a50afea54b","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Every triangle has three interior angles. Call them alpha, beta, and gamma. We’ll show why their sum is always 180 degrees.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Angles in a triangle"},{"op":"figure","id":"triangle","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-1.5,6.8],"y":[-0.6,4],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"a","at":[0,0],"label":"A"},{"kind":"point","id":"b","at":[6,0],"label":"B"},{"kind":"point","id":"c","at":[2,3],"label":"C"},{"kind":"polyline","id":"outline","points":[{"at":"a"},{"at":"b"},{"at":"c"}],"closed":true},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"a"},"from":{"at":"b"},"to":{"at":"c"},"r":0.17,"label":"α"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"b"},"from":{"at":"c"},"to":{"at":"a"},"r":0.17,"label":"β"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"c"},"from":{"at":"a"},"to":{"at":"b"},"r":0.17,"label":"γ"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"997c9ef4-a161-4391-95b5-27a50afea54b","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Draw a line through C parallel to AB. Alternate interior angles copy alpha and beta beside gamma at the top.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"parallel","on":"triangle","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"topline","from":[-1.1,3],"to":[6.4,3],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"c"},"from":[-1.1,3],"to":{"at":"a"},"r":0.22,"label":"α"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"c"},"from":{"at":"b"},"to":[6.4,3],"r":0.22,"label":"β"}]},{"op":"text","id":"reason","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"content":"Parallel lines give equal alternate angles."}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"997c9ef4-a161-4391-95b5-27a50afea54b","step":{"id":"s3","script":"At C, alpha, gamma, and beta fit together into a straight angle. A straight angle is 180 degrees, so the triangle’s angles sum to 180.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"straight","on":"triangle","marks":[{"kind":"arc","center":{"at":"c"},"r":1.35,"start":180,"end":360,"arrow":true},{"kind":"text","at":[2,1.35],"text":"180°","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"sum","anchor":{"el":"reason","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"\\alpha+\\gamma+\\beta=180^\\circ"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"If two angles in a triangle are 50° and 60°, what is the third angle?","expected_gist":"70°, because 180° − 50° − 60° = 70°."}}}
